---
description: Tests and quality gates of ManualKitBundle
globs:
  - "tests/**/*.php"
  - "src/Resources/assets/**/*.test.ts"
  - "demo/symfony8/tests/**/*.php"
  - "demo/symfony8/e2e/**/*.ts"
  - "phpunit.xml.dist"
  - "vitest.config.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

Test layout: `tests/Unit`, `tests/Integration` (kernel boot, `tests/Support/TestKernel.php`), `tests/Functional`
(HTTP + commands), Vitest next to the TypeScript sources, Playwright e2e in `demo/symfony8/e2e`.

When behaviour changes, add or update the nearest test:
- config validation → `tests/Unit/DependencyInjection/ConfigurationTest.php` (data provider of invalid configs)
- providers → `tests/Unit/Translation/ProvidersTest.php` (`MockHttpClient`; an empty `MockResponse` chunk simulates a
  timeout)
- pages → `tests/Functional/ManualControllerTest.php`

Gates (all inside Docker): `make test`, `make test-coverage-100` (PHP 100% lines), `make test-ts`, `make phpstan`
(level 8), `make rector-dry`, `make igor`, `make cs-check`, and `make release-check` for the whole chain.
Fixtures must not contain realistic-looking secrets: use obvious placeholders.
Do not add testing frameworks or rewrite unrelated tests.
